🧠 The report has been generated successfully. Summary of the analysis workflow:

1. **QC**: Confirmed human gene symbols with `MT-` mitochondrial prefix; standard thresholds (min 200 genes/cell, max 5% mito, min 3 cells/gene) fit the data well, removing only 57 cells.
2. **Doublet detection**: Non-bimodal score distribution led to using median+3×MAD (0.1) as threshold, removing 222 cells (8.4%).
3. **Normalization & PCA**: Single clean donor/run justified PCA over scVI batch correction.
4. **Clustering**: Leiden resolution 1.0 yielded 9 clusters spanning all major PBMC lineages.
5. **Annotation**: CellTypist (fine-grained model) assigned 8 cell types, cross-validated against canonical markers (CD3D/CD8A/CD8B for CD8 T cells, CD79A/MS4A1/CD19 for B cells, CD14/LYZ/FCN1 for classical monocytes, FCER1A/CD1C for DCs, GNLY/NKG7/FCGR3A for NK cells, FCGR3A/MS4A7 for non-classical monocytes, PPBP/PF4 for platelets) — all confirmed without contradiction, so no relabeling was needed.
6. Final dataset: 2,421 high-quality annotated cells written to the output `.h5ad`, with a full report including figures and decision tables.

